*----
*  RBMK-1000  --  A5b: MULTICOMPO EXPORT
*
*  THE ARTIFACT THAT CONNECTS DRAGON TO DONJON.  Until this deck ran, nothing
*  in this project had ever written cross sections to disk: every good cell
*  calculation left its result in an in-memory LCM directory that END: threw
*  away, and the DONJON core decks ran on generic IAEA 2-group PWR constants.
*  The lattice work and the core work were not connected at all.
*
*  Geometry, tracking, self-shielding and depletion are exactly those of
*  rbmk_a5_void.x2m and rbmk_cell_a3.x2m; compositions come from
*  rbmk_proc/RbmkLib.c2m, which since 2026-09-23 uses bound H1_H2O.  What is
*  new here is the COMPO: object, the four branch axes, and the export.
*
*  AXES
*    burnup   IRRA          0 -> 20 MWd/kg at 16.7 MW/t
*    DCA      VALU REAL     coolant density 0.72 -> 0.02 g/cm3 -- THE VOID AXIS
*    TF       TEMP MIX 6    fuel temperature -- Doppler
*    TG       TEMP MIX 5    graphite temperature -- RBMK-specific and large
*                           (graphite is 89.6 % of the cell)
*
*  Xe is NOT an axis here.  XENON: in DONJON gives equilibrium xenon only, so
*  an explicit Xe axis is needed eventually for the ORM story, but it
*  multiplies the grid by ~4 and should not delay the first working COMPO.
*  That is A5b.2, after this file is proven to load in DONJON.
*
*  ON THE VOID AXIS AND ITS UNCERTAINTY.  DRAGON and OpenMC agree on the sign
*  and the burnup trend of the void coefficient and disagree on its magnitude
*  by ~2x at discharge burnup and ~12x at fresh fuel (PROGRESS.md, "OpenMC
*  cross-check").  This deck produces the DRAGON side.  A second COMPO, whose
*  void branches are scaled to OpenMC's branch RATIO k_void/k_nom, is built
*  downstream; A8 runs under both.  Nothing here is tuned toward either.
*
*  LEAKAGE MODEL AT ZERO BUCKLING -- why FLU: is not plain TYPE K.
*  COMPO: copies diffusion coefficients into the MULTICOMPO only when the
*  edit object's state vector says a leakage model was used (EDIPXS.f:413-419
*  sets IDATA(9); COMACR.f:91,169 reads it).  EDI: GOLVER writes a 'DIFF'
*  block but does NOT set that flag, so the coefficients are computed and then
*  silently dropped, and DONJON stops at "TRISYS: NO DIFFUSION COEFFICIENTS".
*  So a leakage model is mandatory.  BUCK 0.0 imposes ZERO buckling, which
*  activates the B1 machinery without perturbing the spectrum -- k-infinity
*  must come out bit-identical to the plain TYPE K value (1.310172 fresh), and
*  that identity is checked rather than assumed.  A critical-buckling search
*  (TYPE B B1) would instead reweight the spectrum for ~24 %% leakage, which is
*  wrong for a channel sitting inside a 12.25 m core whose real geometric
*  buckling is ~3e-5 cm-2.
*
*  MICR list: 31 nuclides.  Every name was verified to exist in the DLIB_99
*  depletion chain (rbmk_chainprobe.x2m), and the list was then closed under
*  EDI:'s own lumping rule (rbmk_micrprobe.x2m, driven to a fixed point):
*  EDILUM.f:230-254 refuses to lump any isotope whose maximum fission yield
*  exceeds 1 %% and which is stable or has a half-life over 30 days.  Ru103 is
*  the only one this adds beyond the physically-motivated list.  MICR ALL
*  would instead carry all 299 depleting isotopes at every branch point.
*----
LINKED_LIST LIBRARY LIBSS GEOSS GEOFL TRKSS TRK SYS FLUX BURNUP
            EDIOBJ COMPO DONNEES ;
SEQ_BINARY  FTRKSS FTRK ;
SEQ_ASCII   _ACompo :: FILE './_ACompo' ;
MODULE      LIB: GEO: NXT: USS: ASM: FLU: EVO: EDI: COMPO:
            GREP: DELETE: UTL: END: ;
PROCEDURE   RbmkLib RbmkGeo ;

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  NOMINAL STATE AND BRANCH GRIDS
*--------------------------------------------------------------
REAL tfnom := 900.0 ;   ! K, nominal fuel temperature
REAL tgnom := 750.0 ;   ! K, nominal graphite temperature
REAL tcool :=  573.0 ;  ! K, coolant and structure (saturation at 6.9 MPa)
REAL dnom  :=   0.72 ;  ! g/cm3, nominal coolant density
REAL fpwr  :=   16.7 ;  ! MW per tonne initial heavy metal (3200 MWth / 192 t)

INTEGER nbu := 6 ;
INTEGER ndc := 7 ;
INTEGER ntf := 5 ;
INTEGER ntg := 3 ;

DONNEES := UTL: :: CREA 'burn' <<nbu>> =
   0.0  2000.0  5000.0  10000.0  15000.0  20000.0 ;
DONNEES := UTL: DONNEES :: CREA 'dca' <<ndc>> =
   0.72  0.60  0.45  0.30  0.15  0.05  0.02 ;
DONNEES := UTL: DONNEES :: CREA 'tf' <<ntf>> =
   600.0  900.0  1200.0  1500.0  2000.0 ;
DONNEES := UTL: DONNEES :: CREA 'tg' <<ntg>> =
   500.0  750.0  900.0 ;

INTEGER istep iv itf itg ;
REAL bubeg buend tbeg tend dbr tfbr tgbr kinf ;

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  GEOMETRY AND TRACKING  (identical to rbmk_cell_a3.x2m)
*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  Both geometries come from rbmk_proc/RbmkGeo.c2m, the single source of
*  truth for the cell -- see its header for every dimension and source.
GEOSS GEOFL := RbmkGeo ;
TRKSS FTRKSS := NXT: GEOSS ::
  EDIT 0 TITLE 'RBMK-A5B-SS' ALLG BATCH 100 TISO 8 15.0 ;
TRK   FTRK   := NXT: GEOFL ::
  EDIT 0 TITLE 'RBMK-A5B-FLUX' ALLG BATCH 100 TISO 15 30.0 ;

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  COMPO INITIALIZATION
*    Reference: rep900_mco.x2m:218-247 (declaration) and :944 (export).
*    TF and TG are TEMP axes, so COMPO: reads them from the mixture
*    temperatures of the LIBRARY it is handed -- they are not set by name.
*    DCA has no library counterpart and is set explicitly per branch.
*--------------------------------------------------------------
COMPO := COMPO: ::
  EDIT 1
  STEP UP 'EDIRBMK'
  MAXCAL 5
  COMM 'RBMK-1000 channel cell, 2 wt% U-235, DLIB_99 (ENDF/B-VIII.1)' ENDC
  PARA 'burnup' IRRA
  PARA 'TF'  TEMP LIBRARY 6
  PARA 'TG'  TEMP LIBRARY 5
  PARA 'DCA' VALU REAL
  INIT
  ;

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  REFERENCE DEPLETION AT THE NOMINAL STATE
*--------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO "=== A5b: reference depletion at dca" dnom "TF" tfnom "TG" tgnom "===" ;

LIBRARY := RbmkLib :: <<dnom>> <<tfnom>> <<tgnom>> <<tcool>> ;
LIBSS   := USS: LIBRARY TRKSS FTRKSS :: EDIT 0 PASS 2 GRMIN 18 ;
SYS     := ASM: LIBSS TRK FTRK :: EDIT 0 ;
FLUX    := FLU: LIBSS TRK SYS :: TYPE K B1 SIGS BUCK 0.0 EXTE 1.0E-6 ;
GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-INFINITY' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "A5BREF  BU 0.0  k-inf" kinf ;

EVALUATE tend := 0.0 ;
BURNUP LIBSS := EVO: LIBSS FLUX TRK ::
  EDIT 0 SAVE <<tend>> DAY POWR <<fpwr>> ;

EVALUATE istep := 1 ;
WHILE istep nbu < DO
  EVALUATE istep := istep 1 + ;
  EVALUATE bubeg tbeg := buend tend ;
  GREP: DONNEES :: GETVAL 'burn' <<istep>> >>buend<< ;
  EVALUATE tend := buend fpwr / ;

  BURNUP LIBSS := EVO: BURNUP LIBSS FLUX TRK ::
    EDIT 0 NOEX DEPL <<tbeg>> <<tend>> DAY POWR <<fpwr>> ;

  SYS  := DELETE: SYS ;
  SYS  := ASM: LIBSS TRK FTRK :: EDIT 0 ;
  FLUX := FLU: FLUX LIBSS TRK SYS :: TYPE K B1 SIGS BUCK 0.0 EXTE 1.0E-6 ;
  GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-INFINITY' 1 >>kinf<< ;
  ECHO "A5BREF  BU" buend "  k-inf" kinf ;

  BURNUP LIBSS := EVO: BURNUP LIBSS FLUX TRK ::
    EDIT 0 SAVE <<tend>> DAY POWR <<fpwr>> ;
ENDWHILE ;

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  BRANCH TENSOR AND COMPO FEEDING
*
*  At every burnup point the library is rebuilt at the branch state, the
*  depleted fuel isotopics are restored from the BURNUP object, and the cell
*  is RE-SELF-SHIELDED before being re-solved.  Re-doing USS: per branch is
*  not optional: voiding hardens the spectrum into the U-238 resonances, and
*  that is precisely where self-shielding acts.
*--------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO "" ;
ECHO "=== A5b: branch tensor, DCA x TF x TG at each burnup ===" ;

EVALUATE istep := 0 ;
WHILE istep nbu < DO
  EVALUATE istep := istep 1 + ;
  GREP: DONNEES :: GETVAL 'burn' <<istep>> >>buend<< ;
  EVALUATE tend := buend fpwr / ;

  EVALUATE itg := 0 ;
  WHILE itg ntg < DO
    EVALUATE itg := itg 1 + ;
    GREP: DONNEES :: GETVAL 'tg' <<itg>> >>tgbr<< ;

    EVALUATE itf := 0 ;
    WHILE itf ntf < DO
      EVALUATE itf := itf 1 + ;
      GREP: DONNEES :: GETVAL 'tf' <<itf>> >>tfbr<< ;

      EVALUATE iv := 0 ;
      WHILE iv ndc < DO
        EVALUATE iv := iv 1 + ;
        GREP: DONNEES :: GETVAL 'dca' <<iv>> >>dbr<< ;

        LIBRARY := DELETE: LIBRARY ;
        LIBRARY := RbmkLib :: <<dbr>> <<tfbr>> <<tgbr>> <<tcool>> ;
        LIBRARY := LIB: LIBRARY BURNUP ::
          EDIT 0 BURN <<istep>> MIX 6 MIX 7 ;

        LIBSS := DELETE: LIBSS ;
        LIBSS := USS: LIBRARY TRKSS FTRKSS :: EDIT 0 PASS 2 GRMIN 18 ;
        SYS   := DELETE: SYS ;
        SYS   := ASM: LIBSS TRK FTRK :: EDIT 0 ;
        FLUX  := DELETE: FLUX ;
        FLUX  := FLU: LIBSS TRK SYS :: TYPE K B1 SIGS BUCK 0.0 EXTE 1.0E-6 ;
        GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-INFINITY' 1 >>kinf<< ;
        ECHO "A5BTAB" buend dbr tfbr tgbr kinf ;

        EDIOBJ := EDI: LIBSS TRK FLUX GEOFL SYS ::
          EDIT 0
          MICR 31
            U234  U235  U236  U238  Np237 Np239 Pu238 Pu239 Pu240 Pu241
            Pu242 Am241 Am242m Am243 Cm242 Cm243 Cm244
            Xe135 I135  Sm149 Pm149 Sm151
            Nd143 Ru103 Rh103 Cs133 Tc99  Gd155 Gd157 Eu153 B10
          MERG COMP
          COND 0.625
*         GOLVER asks for diffusion coefficients by the Golfier-Vergain
*         formula, D = 1 / (3 (Sigma_t - Sigma_s1)).  It is NOT sufficient on
*         its own, and the failure is silent:
*           EDIPXS.f:344-351  writes the 'DIFF' block under GOLVER *or* a
*                             leakage model, so the edit object looks right;
*           EDIPXS.f:413-419  sets the state-vector flag IDATA(9) only under
*                             a LEAKAGE MODEL -- GOLVER alone leaves it 0;
*           COMACR.f:91,169   reads NLEAK=IPAR(9) and only then copies 'DIFF'
*                             out of the edit, storing it in the COMPO under
*                             the name 'STRD' (COMACR.f:246).
*         With GOLVER alone the COMPO is written, is a valid L_MULTICOMPO, and
*         has no STRD -- DONJON then stops at "TRISYS: NO DIFFUSION
*         COEFFICIENTS" two hours of CPU later.  That is why every FLU: call in
*         this deck is 'TYPE K B1 SIGS BUCK 0.0': the B1 machinery sets the
*         flag, and imposing ZERO buckling leaves the spectrum untouched, so
*         the k-infinity values cross-checked against OpenMC do not move
*         (measured: 1.310172 -> 1.310173).  GOLVER is kept because it is what
*         supplies the DIFF values the leakage flag then lets through.
*         A critical-buckling search (TYPE B) would also set the flag but WOULD
*         change the condensation spectrum; it is deliberately not used.
          GOLVER
          SAVE ON EDIRBMK
          ;

*       COMPO: finds the microlib BY LCM OBJECT NAME, not by argument
*       position: the token after TEMP in the PARA declaration above is the
*       name of the linked list to read the temperature from (COMGEP.f:135
*       -> COMBIB.f:58-68).  So this must be LIBRARY, not LIBSS.
        COMPO := COMPO: COMPO EDIOBJ BURNUP LIBRARY ::
          EDIT 0
          STEP UP 'EDIRBMK'
          'DCA' <<dbr>>
          SET <<tend>> DAY ;

        EDIOBJ := DELETE: EDIOBJ ;
      ENDWHILE ;
    ENDWHILE ;
  ENDWHILE ;
ENDWHILE ;

*--------------------------------------------------------------
*  EXPORT.  This assignment is the step that had never been done.
*  Without it the database lives in memory and END: discards it.
*  DONJON reads it back with  Cpo := _ACompo ;  (channel_mphy.x2m:52,69).
*--------------------------------------------------------------
_ACompo := COMPO ;

UTL: COMPO :: DIR ;

END: ;
QUIT .
